      "svg": "<rect x=\"40\" y=\"40\" width=\"720\" height=\"420\" fill=\"#0a1326\" stroke=\"#1e293b\" rx=\"12\"/>\n<g class=\"el\" data-beat=\"1\">\n          <text x=\"400\" y=\"80\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mangalyaan — Mars Orbiter Mission (2013)</text>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"105\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Launched by ISRO — smart, low-cost technology</text>\n<circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"240\" r=\"35\" fill=\"#1e6cb0\" stroke=\"#38bdf8\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"295\" fill=\"#38bdf8\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">EARTH</text>\n<text x=\"160\" y=\"312\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">launch site</text>\n<circle cx=\"620\" cy=\"240\" r=\"22\" fill=\"#ef4444\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"620\" y=\"295\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-size=\"12\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">MARS</text>\n<text x=\"620\" y=\"312\" fill=\"#94a3b8\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">edge of habitable zone</text>\n<path d=\"M 195 240 Q 400 150 600 240\" stroke=\"#fbbf24\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"6,4\" fill=\"none\" marker-end=\"url(#arrMY1)\"/>\n<defs><marker id=\"arrMY1\" markerWidth=\"8\" markerHeight=\"8\" refX=\"4\" refY=\"4\" orient=\"auto\"><polygon points=\"0,0 8,4 0,8\" fill=\"#fbbf24\"/></marker></defs>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"170\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-size=\"20\" text-anchor=\"middle\">🛰️</text>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"195\" fill=\"#fbbf24\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Mangalyaan</text>\n        </g>\n<g class=\"el\" data-beat=\"2\">\n          <rect x=\"60\" y=\"340\" width=\"680\" height=\"110\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"rgba(167,139,250,0.10)\" stroke=\"#a78bfa\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"365\" fill=\"#a78bfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What Mangalyaan Studied</text>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"388\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">• Mars atmosphere (is it thick enough? what gases?)</text>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"408\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">• Surface features (signs of past water, maybe lakes)</text>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"428\" fill=\"#cbd5e1\" font-size=\"12\" text-anchor=\"middle\">• Big question: Was Mars ever suitable for life?</text>\n<text x=\"400\" y=\"445\" fill=\"#34d399\" font-size=\"11\" font-weight=\"700\" text-anchor=\"middle\">✓ Showed the world India could do space science with smart, low-cost technology</text>\n        </g>",
      "beats": [
        "In 2013, the Indian Space Research Organisation (ISRO) launched Mangalyaan — also called the Mars Orbiter Mission. It was a historic moment for India and the world. Let us trace its journey.",
        "Mangalyaan was launched from Earth and travelled through space to reach Mars. It carried special tools (sensors) to study the planet's atmosphere, surface, and signs of past water. The big question scientists wanted to answer was: was Mars ever suitable for life?",
        "Mangalyaan showed the world that India could do space science with smart, low-cost technology. Most Mars missions cost billions of dollars, but Mangalyaan was made on a very small budget — and it succeeded! It helped bring Mars closer to all of us. Even though no proof of life has been found yet, the search continues. As we learned: science stays open to new discoveries."
      ]
